# Repo Info

## Environments

Three environments, **local**, **staging**, **prod** set via `ENVIRONMENT`, variable are picked up by manage.py. Default to local for development. Staging and prod configs exist for database seeding and deployment.

## Backend Structure

- `backend/apps/config/` — Environment setup and constants. `base.py` is shared; `local.py`, `staging.py`, `prod.py` override per environment.
- `backend/apps/` — Django apps (cattle, alerts, etc.).
- `backend/ml/` — Inference pipelines, health models, and heavy data processing. Often uses Redis as a cache or ephemeral store.
- `backend/tests/` — pytest suite for GitHub Actions CI. Write tests that stress edge cases and verify expected behavior for any new function, class, or service.

## Frontend Structure

- `frontend/src/components/` — UI components.
- `frontend/src/services/` — API and data-layer code.
- `frontend/src/hooks/` — Custom React hooks.
- `frontend/src/lib/` — Pure utilities and helpers.
- `frontend/src/assets/` — Static images, icons, Lottie JSON.

## Linting & Formatting

- ESLint via `eslint.config.js` — no inline rule disabling except in rare, justified cases.
- Prettier — wrap at 100 chars.
